## Test it

```bash
python -m pytest mcp-servers/{{ name }}
```

The tests need no account and no network. {{ "The API is not called: `" ~ responses_file ~ "` holds what it answers,\nby method and path. " if rest else "" }}They run the real rules file, so
they show what each role is allowed to see:

| Role | Tool call | Data |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `manager` | allowed | every column |
{% if plan.masked %}
| `analyst` | allowed | {% for column in plan.masked %}`{{ column }}`{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %} {{ "is" if plan.masked | length == 1 else "are" }} masked, at most {{ analyst_rows }} rows |
{% else %}
| `analyst` | allowed | every column, at most {{ analyst_rows }} rows |
{% endif %}
| anything else | denied | none |

Start a change with a test in `tests/test_{{ package }}.py`: pick the caller's
roles, call the tool, and say what that caller should be shown.
