## Run it

```bash
{{ name }}        # serves http://127.0.0.1:{{ port }}/mcp, with /healthz and /readyz
```

On this machine a caller without a token is the development identity in
`{{ var.identity_options }}`. Local state is written under `.agentlib/`.
{% if rest %}

Running the server calls the real API at `{{ plan.options.base_url }}`. That
address is the `base_url` of the data source in `.env`. If the API wants a
token:

1. Add `"auth_secret": "{{ plan.source }}_token"` to the data source's options
   in `.env`. The token is sent as a bearer token; `auth_header` and
   `auth_scheme` change that.
2. Set `{{ var.secret_prefix }}{{ plan.source | upper }}_TOKEN` in `.env`, never in
   `.env.example`. When deployed, the secret comes from the secrets provider.
{% endif %}

